tobii-linux @VERSION@: the Linux driver for the Tobii Eye Tracker 5

Install it, as root, from this directory:

    sudo ./install.sh

It copies what files/ holds under / (the programs, libtobii.so and its
headers under /usr/local, the udev rules under /etc/udev/rules.d), adds
/etc/ld.so.conf.d/tobii.conf, reloads udev and enables tobiid.socket for
every user. "Tobii Calibration" then shows among the applications.

Remove it:

    sudo /usr/local/share/tobii-linux/install.sh --uninstall

It needs x86_64, systemd (logind gives the user the tracker, the user units
start the daemon), glibc @GLIBC_MAX@ or newer, libusb-1.0, libudev and the
libstdc++ of GCC 12 or newer: Ubuntu 22.04, Debian 12, Fedora 36 and their
successors, for instance. install.sh checks the libraries before it copies
anything. On Debian, Ubuntu, Fedora and openSUSE the .deb or .rpm is the
easier way.

More in /usr/local/share/doc/tobii-linux/INSTALL.md once installed, or at
https://github.com/Skyggedans/tobii-linux
